<title>NEW ZEALAND: CULTUS SAYS BORAL FARMS INTO OTWAY LICENCE.</title>
<headline>CULTUS SAYS BORAL FARMS INTO OTWAY LICENCE.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cultus Petroleum No Liability, through its wholly owned subsidiary Basin Oil, said on Thursday it had reached an agreement allowing Boral to farm into the onshore South Australian, Otway Basin Licence, PEL-39.</p>
<p>Boral Energy Resources and Oil Company of Australia will jointly earn a 30 percent interest in PEL-39 by contributing to the costs of the East Avenue-1 well.</p>
<p>The well is scheduled for drilling in the last quarter of 1997 or the first quarter of 1998.  </p>
<p>Cultus said interest holders in PEL-39 were:</p>
<p>    Cultus Group	  50 pct</p>
<p>    Boral Group	   30 pct</p>
<p>    Lakes Oil NL	  10 pct</p>
<p>    Sun Resources NL    10 pct</p>
